

1. Setup your .env file
Create the file in your project root (and make sure to add .env to your .gitignore!):
text
WHATSAPP_PRIVATE_KEY_B64=LS0tLS1CRUdJTiBSU0EgUFJJVkFURS...[YOUR_BASE64_STRING]...
Use code with caution.

2. Install the Loader
.NET doesn't read .env files natively. The industry standard is DotNetEnv. DotNetEnv GitHub Repository
Run this command:
dotnet add package DotNetEnv
3. Load and Use in Program.cs
Call the loader at the very top of your Program.cs so the variables are available to your builder.Configuration.
csharp
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;

// 1. Load the .env file into the system environment
DotNetEnv.Env.Load();

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// 2. Access it via Configuration (it looks in Environment Variables automatically)
string? base64Key = builder.Configuration["WHATSAPP_PRIVATE_KEY_B64"];

if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(base64Key))
{
    // 3. Decode and Import
    string pemString = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(Convert.FromBase64String(base64Key));
    using var rsa = RSA.Create();
    rsa.ImportFromPem(pemString);
    
    // Now your RSA object is ready for WhatsApp decryption!
}